   "evidence": "`grep -rn commute_toEnd code/` returns only the three declarations, the Symmetrizer Main-results line 55, the unrelated `Mathematics/LieAlgebra/Casimir.lean` lemmas, and the docstring at SpinDecomposition.lean:28 \u2014 no proof uses them. The two actions are the same expression: `diagEnd A B := A.rTensor N + B.lTensor M` (upstream/Physlib/PhyslibAlpha/Mathematics/RepresentationTheory/Sl2/TensorHighestWeight.lean:72-73) vs `TensorProduct.hasBracketAux x := (toEnd R L M x).rTensor N + (toEnd R L N x).lTensor M` (upstream/mathlib/Mathlib/Algebra/Lie/TensorProduct.lean:46-47, the bracket of `TensorProduct.lieRingModule` at :50), with `Module.End.instLieRingModule` (upstream/mathlib/Mathlib/Algebra/Lie/OfAssociative.lean:118) supplying `L = Module.End \u2102 \u2102\u00b2`; neither Physlib nor TauCeti states the `diagEnd`-form commutation (`grep -rn 'TensorProduct\\.comm' upstream/Physlib` has no such lemma).",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/Mathematics/LinearAlgebra/TensorProduct/Symmetrizer.lean",
   "fix": "Either add the bridge in the physics module \u2014 `LieModule.toEnd \u2102 (Module.End \u2102 \u2102\u00b2) (\u2102\u00b2 \u2297[\u2102] \u2102\u00b2) X = PhyslibAlpha.Sl2.diagEnd X X` \u2014 and derive the channels' invariance under `tensor spinRep spinRep`'s generators from the two `commute_toEnd_*Proj` lemmas, or drop the three lemmas together with the SpinDecomposition docstring claim.",
   "issue": "`commute_toEnd_comm` (line 102) and `commute_toEnd_antisymmProj`/`commute_toEnd_symmProj` (lines 309, 315) state invariance under `x \u2297 1 + 1 \u2297 x` through `LieModule.toEnd` on Mathlib's tensor-product Lie module, while the coupled action this PR uses for the same operator is PhyslibAlpha's located `Sl2.diagEnd` (via `AngularMomentumRepresentation.tensor`). No lemma bridges the two, so the three lemmas have no consumer anywhere in the repo and SpinDecomposition.lean:28 cites `TensorProduct.commute_toEnd_antisymmProj` as establishing that the channels commute with the total-spin action without any declaration connecting it to `(tensor spinRep spinRep)`.",
